    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/pages/jobshome/": {
      "title": "Jobs Listings Home",
      "description": "Jobs Listings Home - Wilkes University Jobs Listings Home Jobs Login At Wilkes University, faculty and staff foster a community dedicated to student success and professional fulfillment. Human Resources supports our most important asset - our people. We strive to make Wilkes a great place to work by recruiting, retaining and developing outstanding employees. Why Work at Wilkes? Wilkes University offers the opportunities of a large university in the mentoring culture of a small college. It's a place where you can achieve your professional and personal best. We believe in employee empowerment, development, accountability and work/life balance. Diversity is one of our core values at Wilkes and we encourage applications from diverse backgrounds. Through a commitment to embracing our differences, we create a more vibrant, inclusive learning community. Located on the Susquehanna River in the heart of Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, our 35-acre campus is a community within a community. You'll find a variety of ways to build your skills and enjoy resources at Wilkes and in the surrounding area. Catch up with colleagues in the dining hall or stroll downtown to grab lunch. Enjoy access to a variety of guest speakers. Browse the Sordoni Art Gallery, cheer on our Division III Colonels and get tickets to student productions at the Dorothy Dickson Darte Center for the Performing Arts. When you want to venture off campus, you can take advantage of northeastern Pennsylvania's opportunities for outdoor adventure. Hiking, camping, and skiing are all nearby. If you want to go further, cultural centers like New York City and Philadelphia are about two hours away. Click the following link to see our current Job Listings Hiring Software Maintained by isolved Talent Acquisition - © 2026 Refresh"
    },
    "https://www.wilkes.edu/admissions/financial-aid/undergraduate-aid/types-of-aid/student-work-study-jobs/index.aspx": {
      "title": "Work Study",
      "description": "Student Work Study Jobs | Wilkes University Wilkes University uses cookies and similar technologies to provide you the best possible\n         experience on our website. For more information, please review our privacy policy . Accept Wilkes University Wilkes University Programs News & Events Alumni Wilkes Portal Request Info Visit Apply Toggle Search and Navigation Menu Wilkes University Request Info Visit Apply Programs News & Events Alumni Wilkes Portal Top Searches Calendars Tuition Graduate Programs Online Programs Virtual Tour Jobs at Wilkes For You Parents Alumni Employers Academics & Research Admission & Financial Aid Life at Wilkes Athletics About Wilkes Give to Wilkes Work Study Home - Admissions - Financial Aid & Scholarships - Undergraduate Financial Aid - Types of Financial Aid - Work Study In this Section Work Study Job Openings Submit a Work Study Job Opening Work Study Private Undergraduate Loans PA State Grant Program Foster Independence Tuition Waiver Program Work study programs allow you to earn money to help pay for your education and related\n                                 expenses while also building your resume. View Work Study Openings Hiring Process For Students The following is for students interested in obtaining a work study position. Work-Study Onboarding Requirements If you are new to Work-Study or have not worked in a Work-Study position within the\n                           past 13 months, you must complete the onboarding process before beginning employment. To receive on boarding instructions and required paperwork, please contact Kimberly\n                           Mazur at kimberly.mazur@wilkes.edu email link to request the onboarding information. You may not begin working until all onboarding requirements have been completed and\n                              approved . If you have held a work-study position at Wilkes within the past 13 month, you will\n                     not need to complete the student work study forms again unless: Your permanent home address has changed Your banking/direct deposit information has changed If either of the above applies, please email workstudy@wilkes.edu email link for further instructions. Before Applying Before applying for a Federal Work Study position, please review your Financial Aid\n                     award for the current academic year to confirm your eligibility. If you have questions\n                     regarding your status, please email workstudy@wilkes.edu email link . Students who are not eligible for Federal Work Study may apply only for positions\n                     funded through Institutional Work Study. Prior to applying, please confirm with the\n                     hiring supervisor that the department has institutional funds available to support\n                     the position. Applying for a Work Study Position Available work study openings are posted below. Before applying, contact the hiring\n                     supervisor to discuss the position requirements and responsibilities. View Current Job Openings For Hiring Supervisors The following is for work study hiring supervisors who wish to hire for student work\n                     study positions. Submitting an Opening Hiring supervisors can submit an opening below. When approved, it will be posted on\n                     the work study openings page. Post a Work Study Position Hiring Process Please do not automatically submit a Work Study application for the student you would\n                        like to hire . To prevent delays in the hiring process and ensure compliance with work study regulations,\n                     please follow the steps below. Submit Student Information Email workstudy@wilkes.edu email link the student's full name and WIN . Confirm Student Eligibility You will receive an email from workstudy@wilkes.edu email link with the student's Federal Work Study eligibility, confirmation on if they must complete\n                              the New Hire Process, and guidance on next steps. Submit Application Once the student has been approved for Work Study, the hiring supervisor will be notified\n                              that they may submit a Work Study application for the student. The application link\n                              will be provided in the approval email. Additional Work Study Information Students can work a maximum of 20 hours per week during the academic year and 30 hours\n                              per week during the summer term. Work cannot occur during class time. A student is permitted to work a maximum of two jobs per term . Pay ranges are based upon a student's grade level. Undergraduate student pay ranges\n                              are from $9.50 to $12.00 per hour. Graduate students are paid $14.00 per hour. Acknowledgment of University Policies Student employees are required to read the below policies . Code of Ethics Confidentiality Computer and Electronic Resource Employment at Will Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination Statement and Grievance Procedures Personal Appearance Wilkes University Drug and Alcohol Abuse Prevention Program Workers' Compensation Insurance Questions? Contact us for any questions about work study. 570-408-4512 workstudy@wilkes.edu email link Wilkes University 1-800-WILKES-U admissions@wilkes.edu Library Human Resources Give to Wilkes Wilkes University on Facebook Wilkes University on TikTok TikTok Wilkes University on Instagram Wilkes University on YouTube You don't have to travel far to go further. Wilkes University is within a few hours' drive from the biggest population centers\n                  in the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic. 84 West South Street Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania 18766 © 2026 Wilkes University Accessibility Consumer Information Legal & Privacy Campus Safety Jobs at Wilkes ©"
    },
